! hocc*oc (1-hydroxypropan-2-one):
! assume primary hs are abstracted, like those in acetaldehyde, c-h bond strength=94.6kcal (bozzelli, 2006), similar to a tertiary c-h
hocc*oc + o2 => ch2co + ch2oh + ho2                 3.00e13   0.00 48200.0           ! tertiary rate from sarathy et al. deg=3
hocc*oc + oh => ch2co + ch2oh + h2o                 1.720e+05 2.400 815.0            ! saudi aramco mech 1.3, acetaldehyde primary rate, 1996tay/rah497-504
hocc*oc + h => ch2co + ch2oh + h2                   2.72e+03   3.10  5210.0          ! saudi aramco mech 1.3, acetaldehyde primary rate !ref:harding j. phys. chem., vol. 114, no. 2, 2010
hocc*oc + o => ch2co + ch2oh + oh                   1.14e6       2.41   1140.0       ! tertiary rate rule, sarathy et al. 2011, deg=3
hocc*oc + ch3 => ch2co + ch2oh + ch4                1.8e-9       6.36    893.0       ! tertiary rate rule, sarathy et al. 2011, deg=3
hocc*oc + ch3o2 => ch2co + ch2oh + ch3o2h           6.2e2        3.12  13190.0       ! tertiary rate rule, sarathy et al. 2011, deg=3
hocc*oc + ch3o => ch2co + ch2oh + ch3oh             6.9e10       0.0    2870.0       ! tertiary rate rule, sarathy et al. 2011, deg=3

