! reaction class 29:  cyclic ether reactions with oh and ho2
! rate constant rules from sarathy et al. 2011
! it is expected that 5-membered cyclic ethers > 4-membered > 3-membered in concentration formed
! these are formed by 7-membered ro2 isomerization, 6-membered and 5 membered respectively
! for some products, isomers are used to avoid including another minor oxygenated species
 
tpgme-o1-3 + oh =>  tc3h5ocho + ch3cho + ch2o + c3h6 + oh + h2o    2.0e12  0.0 0.0      !4-membered cyclic ether. 
tpgme-o1-3 + ho2 => tc3h5ocho + ch3cho + ch2o + c3h6 + oh + h2o2   5.00e12 0.0 1.77e+04 !  
tpgme-o1-4 + oh =>  tc3h5ocho + ch3cho + ch2o + c3h6 + oh + h2o    2.0e12  0.0 0.0      !5-membered cyclic ether:use tc3h5ocho similar molecular structures as in 4-methylene-1,3-dioxolane

tpgme-o1-4 + ho2 => tc3h5ocho + ch3cho + ch2o + c3h6 + oh + h2o2   5.00e12 0.0 1.77e+04 !   
tpgme-o1-5 + oh =>  sc3h5ocho + ch3cho + ch2o + c3h6 + oh + h2o    2.0e12  0.0 0.0      !5-membered cyclic ether
tpgme-o1-5 + ho2 => sc3h5ocho + ch3cho + ch2o + c3h6 + oh + h2o2   5.00e12 0.0 1.77e+04 !
           
tpgme-o3-4 + oh  => tc3h5ocho + ch3cho + ch2o + c3h6 + oh + h2o      2.0e12  0.0 0.0      !3-membered cyclic ether. use isomer tc3h5cho instead of 2-methoxyacrylaldehyde, c*c(oc)c*o
tpgme-o3-4 + ho2 => tc3h5ocho + ch3cho + ch2o + c3h6 + oh + h2o2     5.00e12 0.0 1.77e+04 !                         use isomer tc3h5cho instead of 2-methoxyacrylaldehyde, c*c(oc)c*o
