!reaction class 30:  decomposition of large carbonyl species and carbonyl radical species

! from butanols mechanism, sarathy et al. cnf2012:

!class 30 miscellaneous reactions
hoch2cho + o2  =  hoch2co+ho2  2.000e+13  0.50  4.220e+04  
hoch2cho + oh  =  hoch2co+h2o  2.690e+10  0.76 -3.400e+02
hoch2cho+h  =  hoch2co+h2      4.000e+13  0.00  4.200e+03
hoch2cho+o  =  hoch2co + oh    5.000e+12  0.00  1.790e+03
hoch2cho+ho2  =  hoch2co+h2o2  2.800e+12  0.00  1.360e+04
hoch2cho+ch3  =  hoch2co+ch4   1.700e+12  0.00  8.440e+03
hoch2cho+ch3o  =  hoch2co+ch3oh    1.150e+11  0.00  1.280e+03
hoch2cho+ch3o2  =  hoch2co+ch3o2h  1.000e+12  0.00  9.500e+03
hoch2co  =  ch2oh+co  1.000e+11  0.00  9.600e+03


! for tc3h5ocho, assume that the formyl hydrogen is abstracted and then co2
! and c3h5 propenyl radical is formed.
! assume products formed based on formyl h being abstracted.
! included all easily abstractable hs for total rate of abstraction.
! tc3h5ocho has 1 formyl h and 3 primary allylic hs.  use rate primary allylic
! rate rule with a degeneracy of 4
! used rate of c3h6+r=c2h5-a+rh.  multiplied a-factor by 4/3:
tc3h5ocho + o2  =>  co2 + c3h5-t +ho2  4.000e+13  0.00  3.910e+04       !  saudi aramco mech 1.3 (no reference)
tc3h5ocho + oh  =>  co2 + c3h5-t +h2o  4.16e+06   2.0   -298.0          !  tsang 1991  
tc3h5ocho+h     =>  co2 + c3h5-t +h2    2.310e+05 2.50  2492.0          !  tsang 1991  
tc3h5ocho+o     =>  co2 + c3h5-t + oh  2.33e12   0.70  5884.0           !  tsang 1991
tc3h5ocho+ho2   =>  co2 + c3h5-t +h2o2  1.28e+04  2.6    1.39e+04       ! tsang, propene, 1991
tc3h5ocho+ch3   =>  co2 + c3h5-t +ch4   2.95      3.5    5675.0         ! tsang, propene, 1991
tc3h5ocho + ch3o2  =>  co2 + c3h5-t + ch3o2h      1.28e+04   2.6    1.39e+04       ! use ho2 abstraction rate constant

tc3h5ocho+ch3o  =>  co2 + c3h5-t +ch3oh           1.1e11 0.0 2600.0 !! used secondary alkyl h rate for n-alkane+ch3o,
      ! reduced ea by difference between bd for seconary alkyl and primary allylic with f=.2: 0.2(98.4-88.2)=.2*10.2=2.0 
      !est. f is larger than oh which is 0.1.  reduced a factor by 2.6 for tying up rotor (used scott and walkers, c&f2002 a-factors to get 2.6)

! for sc3h5cho, assume that the formyl hydrogen is abstracted and them co2
! and s-c3h5 propenyl radical is formed.
! assume products formed based on formyl h being abstracted.
! included all easily abstractable hs for total rate of abstraction.
! sc3h5ocho has 1 formyl h and 3 primary allylic hs.  use rate primary allylic
! rate rule with a degeneracy of 4
! used rate of c3h6+r=c2h5-a+rh.  multiplied a-factor by 4/3:
sc3h5ocho + o2  =>  co2 + c3h5-s +ho2  4.000e+13  0.00  3.910e+04     !  saudi aramco mech 1.3 (no reference)
sc3h5ocho + oh  =>  co2 + c3h5-s +h2o  4.16e+06   2.0   -298.0        !  tsang 1991  
sc3h5ocho+h  =>  co2 + c3h5-s +h2      2.310e+05 2.50  2492.0         !  tsang 1991  
sc3h5ocho+o  =>  co2 + c3h5-s + oh    2.33e12   0.70  5884.0          !  tsang 1991
sc3h5ocho+ho2  =>  co2 + c3h5-s +h2o2  1.28e+04 2.6    1.39e+04       ! tsang, propene, 1991
sc3h5ocho+ch3  =>  co2 + c3h5-s +ch4   2.95     3.5    5675.0         ! tsang, propene, 1991
sc3h5ocho + ch3o2  =>  co2 + c3h5-s + ch3o2h    1.28e+04   2.6    1.39e+04       ! use ho2 abstraction rate constant

sc3h5ocho+ch3o  =>  co2 + c3h5-s + ch3oh   1.1e11 0.0 2600.0 !! used secondary alkyl h rate for n-alkane+ch3o,
      ! reduced ea by difference between bd for seconary alkyl and primary allylic with f=.2: 0.2(98.4-88.2)=.2*10.2=2.0 
      !est. f is larger than oh which is 0.1.  reduced a factor by 2.6 for tying up rotor (used scott and walkers, c&f2002 a-factors to get 2.6)
      
! for tc3h5och3, assume that the formyl hydrogen is abstracted and them ch2o
! and c3h5 propenyl radical is formed.
! assume products formed based on ether hs being abstracted.
! included all easily abstractable hs for total rate of abstraction.
! tc3h5ocho has 3 primary ether hs and 3 primary allylic hs.  use rate primary allylic
! rate rule with a degeneracy of 6
! used rate of c3h6+r=c2h5-a+rh.  multiplied a-factor by 2:
tc3h5och3 + o2  =>  ch2o + c3h5-s +ho2  6.000e+13  0.00  3.910e+04     !  saudi aramco mech 1.3 (no reference)
tc3h5och3 + oh  =>  ch2o + c3h5-s +h2o  6.16e+06   2.0   -298.0        !  tsang 1991  
tc3h5och3 + h   =>  ch2o + c3h5-s +h2      3.460e+05 2.50  2492.0         !  tsang 1991  
tc3h5och3 + o   =>  ch2o + c3h5-s + oh     3.50e12   0.70  5884.0         !  tsang 1991
tc3h5och3 + ho2  =>  ch2o + c3h5-s +h2o2   1.92e+04 2.6    1.39e+04       ! tsang, propene, 1991
tc3h5och3 + ch3  =>  ch2o + c3h5-s + ch4   4.42     3.5    5675.0         ! tsang, propene, 1991
tc3h5och3 + ch3o2  =>  ch2o + c3h5-s + ch3o2h   1.92e+04   2.6    1.39e+04       ! use ho2 abstraction rate constant

tc3h5och3+ch3o  =>  ch2o + c3h5-s +ch3oh   1.7e11 0.0 2600.0 !! used secondary alkyl h rate for n-alkane+ch3o,
      ! reduced ea by difference between bd for secondary alkyl and primary allylic with f=.2: 0.2(98.4-88.2)=.2*10.2=2.0 
      !est. f is larger than oh which is 0.1.  reduced a factor by 2.6 for tying up rotor (used scott and walkers, c&f2002 a-factors to get 2.6)
      
! for ac3h5och2oh, assume that the ether hydrogen is abstracted and then hocho hydroxyformyl
! and c3h5 propenyl radical is formed.
! assume products formed based on ether h being abstracted.
! included all easily abstractable hs for total rate of abstraction.
! tc3h5och2oh has 2 ether h and 2 primary allylic hs.  use rate primary allylic
! rate rule with a degeneracy of 4
! used rate of c3h6+r=c2h5-a+rh.  multiplied a-factor by 4/3:
ac3h5och2oh + o2  =>  hocho + c3h5-s + ho2  4.000e+13  0.00  3.910e+04     !  saudi aramco mech 1.3 (no reference)
ac3h5och2oh + oh  =>  hocho + c3h5-s + h2o  4.16e+06   2.0   -298.0        !  tsang 1991  
ac3h5och2oh+h  =>  hocho + c3h5-s + h2      2.310e+05 2.50  2492.0         !  tsang 1991  
ac3h5och2oh+o  =>  hocho + c3h5-s + oh      2.33e12   0.70  5884.0         !  tsang 1991
ac3h5och2oh+ho2  =>  hocho + c3h5-s + h2o2  1.28e+04 2.6    1.39e+04       ! tsang, propene, 1991
ac3h5och2oh+ch3  =>  hocho + c3h5-s + ch4   2.95     3.5    5675.0         ! tsang, propene, 1991
ac3h5och2oh+ch3o2  =>  hocho + c3h5-s + ch3o2h   1.28e+04 2.6    1.39e+04       ! use ho2 abstraction rate constant
ac3h5och2oh+ch3o  =>  hocho + c3h5-s + ch3oh     1.1e11 0.0 2600.0 !! used secondary alkyl h rate for n-alkane+ch3o,
      ! reduced ea by difference between bd for secondary alkyl and primary allylic with f=.2: 0.2(98.4-88.2)=.2*10.2=2.0 
      !est. f is larger than oh which is 0.1.  reduced a factor by 2.6 for tying up rotor (used scott and walkers, c&f2002 a-factors to get 2.6)
      !uf=30.

! for ch3o-sc2h4cho, 2-methoxypropanal, consider abstaction of ether hs, primary chs and aldehydic chs:
! use 1/2 of dme abstraction rates:

ch3o-sc2h4cho + o2    =>  ch2o + ch3chcho + ho2        4.1e+13   0.00 44910.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3
ch3o-sc2h4cho + oh    =>  ch2o + ch3chcho + h2o        3.2e+06   2.00  -651.7    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3, arif m, et al., j. phys. chem. a, 101, 13, 2436-2441 (1997)  
ch3o-sc2h4cho + h     =>  ch2o + ch3chcho + h2         3.9e+06   2.09  3384.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3, curran fit to nist database  
ch3o-sc2h4cho + o     =>  ch2o + ch3chcho + oh         3.9e+08   1.36  2250.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3, curran fit to nist database
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ho2   =>  ch2o + ch3chcho + h2o2       4.3e+02   3.01 12090.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3, based on j. aguilera-iparraguirre et al 2008
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ch3   =>  ch2o + ch3chcho + ch4        7.2e-07   5.73  5700.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3, no ref given
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ch3o2 =>  ch2o + ch3chcho + ch3o2h     1.56e+02  3.12 13190.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ch3o  =>  ch2o + ch3chcho + ch3oh      3.00e+11  0.00  4074.0    ! estimate

! use primary alkane abstraction rates, deg=3, take from sarathy et al. 2011:

ch3o-sc2h4cho + o2  =>  ch3o + c2h3cho + ho2  3.0e+13  0.00  5.29e+04     
ch3o-sc2h4cho + oh  =>  ch3o + c2h3cho + h2o  5.3e+09    0.97  1587.0     
ch3o-sc2h4cho + h  =>  ch3o + c2h3cho + h2    6.7e+05    2.54  6756.0     
ch3o-sc2h4cho + o  =>  ch3o + c2h3cho + oh    9.8e+05    2.43  4750.0     
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ho2  =>  ch3o + c2h3cho + h2o2 2.0e+01   3.59  17160.0  
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ch3  =>  ch3o + c2h3cho + ch4  4.5e-01   3.65   7154.0    
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ch3o2  =>  ch3o + c2h3cho + ch3o2h  6.9e-1  3.97 18280.0   
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ch3o  =>  ch3o + c2h3cho + ch3oh  2.2e11 0.00 6458.0   

! use aldehydic abstraction rates, 
! for the formyl h (deg=1): (use acetaldehyde as a model compound).

ch3o-sc2h4cho + o2    => ccjoc + co + ho2   3.000e+13  0.00  3.910e+04 ! saudi aramco mech 1.3
ch3o-sc2h4cho + oh    => ccjoc + co + h2o   3.370e+12  0.00  -619.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3
ch3o-sc2h4cho + h     => ccjoc + co + h2    1.310e+05  2.58  1220.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref:harding j. phys. chem., vol. 114, no. 2, 2010
ch3o-sc2h4cho + o     => ccjoc + co + oh    5.940e+12  0.00  1868.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref:curran, fit to nist database 
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ho2   => ccjoc + co + h2o2  3.01e+12   0.00 11920.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref:baulch et al., j. phys. chem. ref data, 21:411 (1992)
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ch3   => ccjoc + co + ch4   7.080e-04  4.58  1966.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref: gupte et al.,proc combust inst 31 (2007) 167-174
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ch3o2 => ccjoc + co + ch3o2h 3.01e+12   0.00 11920.0    ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref:baulch et al., j. phys. chem. ref data, 21:411 (1992)
ch3o-sc2h4cho + ch3o  => ccjoc + co + ch3oh 2.8e10     0.0   2600.0    ! use primary allylic rate rule, since the c-h bond strength is similar (88-89 kcal/mole)
                 !used secondary alkyl h rate for n-alkane+ch3o,
                 ! reduced ea by difference between bd for secondary alkyl and primary allylic with f=.2: 0.2(98.4-88.2)=.2*10.2=2.0 
                 !est. f is larger than oh which is 0.1.  reduced a factor by 2.6 for tying up rotor (used scott and walkers, c&f2002 a-factors to get 2.6)
                 !uf=30.

! for sc3h5oh, assume that the allyl hydrogen is abstracted and then c2h3cho + h are formed.
! use rate primary allylic
! used rate of c3h6+r=c2h5-a+rh.  
! duplicates earlier in aramco mech:
!sc3h5oh + o2   =>  c2h3cho + h + ho2        3.000e+13  0.00  3.910e+04      !  saudi aramco mech 1.3 (no reference)
!sc3h5oh + oh   =>  c2h3cho + h + h2o        3.1e+06   2.0   -298.0          !  tsang 1991  
!sc3h5oh + h    =>  c2h3cho + h + h2         1.73e+05  2.50   2492.0         !  tsang 1991  
!sc3h5oh + o    =>  c2h3cho + h + oh         1.75e12   0.70   5884.0         !  tsang 1991
!sc3h5oh + ho2  =>  c2h3cho + h + h2o2       9.6e+03   2.6    1.39e+04       ! tsang, propene, 1991
!sc3h5oh + ch3  =>  c2h3cho + h + ch4        2.21      3.5    5675.0         ! tsang, propene, 1991
!sc3h5oh + ch3o2  =>  c2h3cho + h + ch3o2h   9.6e+03   2.6    1.39e+04       ! use ho2 abstraction rate constant
!sc3h5oh+ch3o  =>  c2h3cho + h + ch3oh  8.3e10 0.0 2600.0 !! used secondary alkyl h rate for n-alkane+ch3o,
      ! reduced ea by difference between bd for seconary alkyl and primary allylic with f=.2: 0.2(98.4-88.2)=.2*10.2=2.0 
      !est. f is larger than oh which is 0.1.  reduced a factor by 2.6 for tying up rotor (used scott and walkers, c&f2002 a-factors to get 2.6)
      
! enol-aldehyde isomerization:
! from propanol, man et al. cnf2013:
!sc3h5oh+ho2   = c2h5cho+ho2     1.490e+05  1.67   6.810e+03   !dasilva, bozzelli, chem. phys. lett. 483 (2009) 25–29.
!sc3h5oh+hocho = c2h5cho+hocho   2.81e-02  3.286  -4509.0      !dasilva, angew. chem. 122 (2010) 7685–7687
!sc3h5oh       = c2h5cho         8.59e+11  0.318 5.59e4        !sarathy et al. cnf2012

! for ac3h5oh, assume that the allyl hydrogen is abstracted and then c2h3cho + h are formed.
! use rate secondary allylic rate rule, degeneracy=2
ac3h5oh + o2   =>  c2h3cho + h + ho2        3.000e+13  0.00  3.910e+04      !  saudi aramco mech 1.3 (no reference)
ac3h5oh + oh   =>  c2h3cho + h + h2o        3.17e+06   2.00 -1434.0         ! rate rule for secondary allylic h, heyberger et al., oxidation of small alkenes, ijck 34:666-677 2002. 
                                                                           ! estimated uncertainty factor => 1.5
ac3h5oh + h    =>  c2h3cho + h + h2         5.0e+04   2.5   -1912.0         ! rate rule for secondary allylic h, heyberger et al., oxidation of small alkenes, ijck 34:666-677 2002.
ac3h5oh + o    =>  c2h3cho + h + oh         7.96e+10 0.70    3107.0         ! rate rule for secondary allylic h, heyberger et al., oxidation of small alkenes, ijck 34:666-677 2002). estimated uncertainty factor = 1.5
ac3h5oh + ho2  =>  c2h3cho + h + h2o2       6.80e+03 2.50   10114.0         ! rate rule for seconary allylic h, scott and walker, addition of toluene, combustion and flame 129:365–377 (2002).  estimated based on ethylbenzene+ho2 
ac3h5oh + ch3  =>  c2h3cho + h + ch4        1.48e+00 3.50     4046.0        ! wjp: used primary rate rule from allylic h, heyberger et al., oxidation of small alkenes, ijck 34:666-677 2002). 
!            lowered ea by 0.65(bd primary allyllic - secondary allyllic). 0.65 is for ch3 abstractions reactions from dean and bozzelli combustion chemistry of nitrogen, 1997.  
!            estimated uncertainty factor = 3
ac3h5oh + ch3o2  =>  c2h3cho + h + ch3o2h   6.80e+03 2.50    10114.0         ! use ho2 abstraction rate constant

ac3h5oh + ch3o  =>  c2h3cho + h + ch3oh  4.23e+10 0.00 2400.0  ! used secondary alkyl h rate.   reduce ea by difference between bd for seconary alkyl and secondary allylic with f=.2: 0.2(98.4-85.6)=.2*12.8=2.6  
   ! est. f is larger than oh which is 0.1.  reduced a factor by 2.6 for tying up rotor (used scott and walkers, c&f2002 a-factors to get 2.6)
      
! enol-aldehyde isomerization for ac3h5oh does not occur (oh is not next to c=c):

! for ch3cocho (2-oxopopanal), inlcude two product channels, one for the formyl h being abstracted and the other for the primary c-hs.
