ch3cocho + oh   =>  ch3co + co + h2o         3.370e+12  0.00  -619.0      ! saudi aramco mech 1.3                                                                          
ch3cocho + h    =>  ch3co + co + h2          1.310e+05  2.58  1220.0      ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref:harding j. phys. chem., vol. 114, no. 2, 2010
ch3cocho + o    =>  ch3co + co + oh          5.940e+12  0.00  1868.0      ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref:curran, fit to nist database
ch3cocho + ho2  =>  ch3co + co + h2o2        3.010e+12  0.00  11920.0     ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref:baulch et al., j. phys. chem. ref data, 21:411 (1992)
ch3cocho + ch3  =>  ch3co + co + ch4         7.080e-04  4.58  1966.0      ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref: gupte et al.,proc combust inst 31 (2007) 167-174 
ch3cocho + ch3o2 =>  ch3co + co + ch3o2h    3.01e+12   0.00  11920.0     ! saudi aramco mech 1.3 !ref:baulch et al., j. phys. chem. ref data, 21:411 (1992)
ch3cocho + ch3o  =>  ch3co + co + ch3oh         2.8e10     0.0    2600.0     ! use primary allylic rate rule, since the c-h bond strength is similar (88-89 kcal/mole)
                                                                           !used secondary alkyl h rate for n-alkane+ch3o,
                                                                           ! reduced ea by difference between bd for secondary alkyl and primary allylic with f=.2: 0.2(98.4-88.2)=.2*10.2=2.0 
